{
  "schema": "morphic/schema-labels/1",
  "purpose": "AT-02 ground truth: per-field dtype and semantic role for every valid fixture.",
  "labelledBy": "hand, from the file contents \u2014 never from the profiler's output",
  "rules": [
    "dtype is what the bytes justify, not what would be convenient. A date whose day/month order is unresolved is utf8; a resolved one is timestamp.",
    "role is what the field MEANS. A utf8 column of CLF timestamps is still temporal; an int column of HTTP status codes is a dimension, because averaging it is meaningless.",
    "identifier means the value identifies a row/entity (ids, pids, ordinals). Uniqueness in a small sample is not evidence of identity: latency_ms and qty are measures.",
    "text means an opaque payload a user reads, not a category a user groups by.",
    "A boolean is a two-valued dimension.",
    "Where a label is genuinely debatable the file carries a note saying why. These labels are meant to be argued with; changing one is a reviewable edit, not a silent fix."
  ],
  "targets": {
    "dtypeAccuracy": 0.95,
    "roleAccuracy": 0.85
  },
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "valid/access.log",
      "format": "log",
      "fields": {
        "time": {
          "dtype": "utf8",
          "role": "temporal"
        },
        "host": {
          "dtype": "utf8",
          "role": "dimension"
        },
        "ident": {
          "dtype": "null",
          "role": "unknown"
        },
        "authuser": {
          "dtype": "utf8",
          "role": "dimension"
        },
        "message": {
          "dtype": "utf8",
          "role": "text"
        },
        "status": {
          "dtype": "int64",
          "role": "dimension"
        },
        "bytes": {
          "dtype": "int64",
          "role": "measure"
        },
        "referer": {
          "dtype": "utf8",
          "role": "dimension"
        },
        "user_agent": {
          "dtype": "utf8",
          "role": "dimension"
        }
      },
      "note": "CLF time stays utf8 by design (month names, no ISO); the ROLE is still temporal. HTTP status is a category, not a quantity: averaging status codes is meaningless. The RFC1413 ident field is '-' on every line: there is no data, so null and unknown are the honest answers. The first scorecard caught this label being wrong, not the engine."
    },
    {
      "path": "valid/ambiguous_dates.csv",
      "format": "csv",
      "fields": {
        "booked_on": {
          "dtype": "utf8",
          "role": "temporal"
        },
        "amount": {
          "dtype": "int64",
          "role": "measure"
        }
      },
      "note": "Day/month order is unresolved, so utf8 is the correct dtype. The field is still a date."
    },
    {
      "path": "valid/day_first_dates.csv",
      "format": "csv",
      "fields": {
        "shipped_on": {
          "dtype": "timestamp",
          "role": "temporal"
        },
        "amount": {
          "dtype": "int64",
          "role": "measure"
        }
      },
      "note": "25/12 resolves the order, so this one really is a timestamp."
    },
    {
      "path": "valid/events.jsonl",
      "format": "jsonl",
      "fields": {
        "ts": {
          "dtype": "timestamp",
          "role": "temporal"
        },
        "event": {
          "dtype": "utf8",
          "role": "dimension"
        },
        "latency_ms": {
          "dtype": "int64",
          "role": "measure"
        },
        "user.city": {
          "dtype": "utf8",
          "role": "dimension"
        }
      },
      "note": "latency_ms happens to be unique across these five rows; it is still a measure, not a key."
    },
    {
      "path": "valid/headerless.csv",
      "format": "csv",
      "fields": {
        "column_1": {
          "dtype": "int64",
          "role": "measure"
        },
        "column_2": {
          "dtype": "float64",
          "role": "measure"
        },
        "column_3": {
          "dtype": "int64",
          "role": "measure"
        }
      },
      "note": "No header and no evidence of identity, so the numeric columns are measures."
    },
    {
      "path": "valid/latin1.csv",
      "format": "csv",
      "fields": {
        "name": {
          "dtype": "utf8",
          "role": "dimension"
        },
        "city": {
          "dtype": "utf8",
          "role": "dimension"
        }
      },
      "note": "Two rows: too little evidence to call a name column identifying."
    },
    {
      "path": "valid/logfmt.log",
      "format": "log",
      "fields": {
        "time": {
          "dtype": "timestamp",
          "role": "temporal"
        },
        "level": {
          "dtype": "utf8",
          "role": "severity"
        },
        "service": {
          "dtype": "utf8",
          "role": "dimension"
        },
        "message": {
          "dtype": "utf8",
          "role": "text"
        },
        "latency_ms": {
          "dtype": "int64",
          "role": "measure"
        },
        "retry": {
          "dtype": "bool",
          "role": "dimension"
        }
      },
      "note": "A boolean flag is a two-valued category. retry appears on one line only."
    },
    {
      "path": "valid/mixed_types.csv",
      "format": "csv",
      "fields": {
        "id": {
          "dtype": "int64",
          "role": "identifier"
        },
        "name": {
          "dtype": "utf8",
          "role": "dimension"
        },
        "amount": {
          "dtype": "float64",
          "role": "measure"
        },
        "active": {
          "dtype": "bool",
          "role": "dimension"
        },
        "ts": {
          "dtype": "timestamp",
          "role": "temporal"
        }
      },
      "note": "name is a person label you would group by, not a key; five unique names in five rows is an artefact of the sample size."
    },
    {
      "path": "valid/naive_timestamps.csv",
      "format": "csv",
      "fields": {
        "when": {
          "dtype": "timestamp",
          "role": "temporal"
        },
        "reading": {
          "dtype": "int64",
          "role": "measure"
        }
      },
      "note": "No offset: typed as timestamp with the UTC assumption disclosed."
    },
    {
      "path": "valid/nested.json",
      "format": "json",
      "fields": {
        "id": {
          "dtype": "int64",
          "role": "identifier"
        },
        "user.city": {
          "dtype": "utf8",
          "role": "dimension"
        },
        "user.geo.lat": {
          "dtype": "float64",
          "role": "measure"
        },
        "user.geo.lon": {
          "dtype": "float64",
          "role": "measure"
        },
        "tags": {
          "dtype": "utf8",
          "role": "text"
        },
        "a.b.c.d": {
          "dtype": "utf8",
          "role": "text"
        }
      },
      "note": "tags is an array retained as JSON text; a.b.c.d sits at the depth cap and is retained as JSON text. Both are opaque payloads, not categories to group by."
    },
    {
      "path": "valid/notes.txt",
      "format": "txt",
      "fields": {
